.TH buckle-broker 1  "buckle-broker 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
buckle\-broker \- Buckle: Audited Hardware & macOS Capability Broker for AI Agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbuckle\-broker\fR [\fB\-v \fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Buckle: Audited Hardware & macOS Capability Broker for AI Agents
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Print version information (\-v)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
buckle\-broker\-serial(1)
List active serial ports (/dev/cu.*)
.TP
buckle\-broker\-usb(1)
Inspect connected USB device tree
.TP
buckle\-broker\-notify(1)
Post a safe native macOS user notification
.TP
buckle\-broker\-status(1)
Query system battery and load telemetry
.TP
buckle\-broker\-clip(1)
Clipboard read/write operations
.TP
buckle\-broker\-mcp(1)
Run Model Context Protocol (MCP) stdio server
.TP
buckle\-broker\-version(1)
Print version information
.TP
buckle\-broker\-completions(1)
Generate shell autocompletion script (bash, zsh, fish, powershell)
.TP
buckle\-broker\-man(1)
Render Unix roff man page documentation to stdout
.TP
buckle\-broker\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
